<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down on limited plant purchases.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down on limited plant purchases.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell 100 to 150 rupees a tonne in central Indian markets on limited purchases from processing plants which are losing 500-700 rupees per tonne on processing, due to the high price of soybean.</p>
<p>Business was dull and the undertone was easy. Soyoil solvent prices were down 100 rupees a tonne on selling pressure from solvent plants. Soyoil refined was steady. Business was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were slightly down in export trading. Soymeal yellow was $282-283 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $122 per tonne for ready shipment and was $115 per tonne for March-April delivery in exports.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,250 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,200 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. Trading activity was very dull in export. The undertone was steady.</p>
